Subject: host build: copy semver and picomatch into the release

Why: since upstream 4ee0876 the Host shares the Pi package modules, which load
semver and picomatch through createRequire. The release build only copies
packages the bundler sees as imports, so the Host exited at startup with
"Cannot find module 'semver'". Lists both with the other packages loaded
through createRequire. Same code as the upstream PR.
Upstream: issue https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/issues/10587, PR https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/pull/10589
Remove when: the PR (or another fix for the issue) is merged and upstream.lock moves past it.

diff --git a/apps/host/scripts/build.mjs b/apps/host/scripts/build.mjs
index 9c06e2aa42..0aa2a1d0b0 100644
--- a/apps/host/scripts/build.mjs
+++ b/apps/host/scripts/build.mjs
@@ -244,6 +244,10 @@ try {
   packages.set('node-pty', packageRoot('node-pty', desktopRequire));
   packages.set('sharp', packageRoot('sharp', desktopRequire));
   packages.set('playwright-core', packageRoot('playwright-core', hostRequire));
+  // The shared Pi package modules load these through createRequire, which the
+  // bundler cannot see, so they would otherwise be missing from the release.
+  packages.set('semver', packageRoot('semver', desktopRequire));
+  packages.set('picomatch', packageRoot('picomatch', desktopRequire));
   for (const [name, source] of packages) {
     const ancestors = new Map(packages);
     ancestors.delete(name);
